	(text "USB CONSOLE SERVER - 16 RS-232 console ports per board, three identical boards -> 48 ports on one Pi.\nBoard identity is two solder straps on the MCU sheet; nothing else differs between builds.\nSignal: USB-C -> USB2514B hub -> 4x FT4232H -> 8x MAX3232E -> 16x RJ45 (Cisco console, 3-wire).\nPower: 24 V cabinet bus -> fuse / reverse-block / TVS -> 5 V (Pi), 3.3 V (logic), LM317 3.3 V (MCU)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 22 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b08da08e-b64f-5a46-8745-a1eb0e50fa5c")
	)
	(text "FT1..FT4: one FT4232H cluster per hub port. FT1 serves P01-P04 and sits at the port-01 end of the board.\nPorts are numbered by physical jack; udev symlinks and silkscreen use the same numbers."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 175 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "b132a2c7-2e58-544f-9089-028e126f96f6")
	)
	(text "H1-H4: slotted chassis mounts (the boards are located by the chassis, not the connectors).\nH5-H8: Raspberry Pi HAT pattern, 58 x 49 mm."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30 255 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "cf8872db-f393-556b-add8-cb2446357180")
	)
